# Nerkhnama build-time configuration (all optional).
#
# Values here are read by Gradle at BUILD time and compiled into `BuildConfig`.
# They are NOT read at runtime: Android app processes never inherit shell environment
# variables, so `System.getenv(...)` inside the app would always be empty.
#
# EIA_API_KEY: Optional U.S. Energy Information Administration (EIA API v2) key. When present it
# enables the official Brent (RBRTE) / WTI (RWTC) daily spot benchmark used to cross-check the
# keyless live feeds (Yahoo Finance, CNBC). Leave empty to keep the feature disabled.
#
# Pass it as an environment variable or a Gradle property when building:
#   EIA_API_KEY=your_key ./gradlew :app:assembleRelease
#   ./gradlew :app:assembleRelease -PeiaApiKey=your_key
#
# Never commit real keys: keep them in a local `.env` (git-ignored) or in CI secrets.
# EIA_API_KEY=
